---
layout: base.njk
scripts: true
---

<header class="container">
  <div class="hero-content">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <hgroup>
        <h1>
          {% image "/assets/logo.svg", "WaveFEM Logo", "hero-logo" %}Wave<i
            style="color: black;"
            >FEM</i
          >
        </h1>
        <p>
          Fast, Parametric and Accurate 3D High Frequency Electromagnetic
          Simulation Software
        </p>
      </hgroup>
      <b
        >Register for beta
        <a href="https://forms.gle/afSVpRJ9cY3LF54w8">here</a>!</b
      >
    </div>
    <div class="hero-image">
      {% image "/assets/Hero Horn Sim.webp", "Hero Horn Sim", "hero-img" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<section id="features" class="features-section">
  <div class="container" data-theme="dark">
    <h2>Features</h2>
    <div class="features-grid">
      <article>
        {% image "/assets/features/fast.svg", "Lightning Fast", "feature-icon", "", "lazy" %}
        <h3>Lightning Fast Simulations</h3>
        <p>
          Adaptive meshing and adaptive frequency sweeps solve only what is
          needed.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        {% image "/assets/features/parametric.svg", "Parametric Design", "feature-icon", "", "lazy" %}
        <h3>Parametric Design</h3>
        <p>
          Script geometry in Python, change parameters live and compare design
          variants.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        {% image "/assets/features/integration.svg", "Seamless Integration", "feature-icon", "", "lazy" %}
        <h3>Seamless Integration</h3>
        <p>
          Import .step, .gds and .dxf files, or CadQuery scripts. Export
          Touchstone files.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="interface">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Clean Interface</h2>
    <p>All the functionality is a couple of clicks away...</p>
    <div class="image-container">
      {% image "/assets/gui/gui1.webp", "Gallery Image", "", "gallery-image" %}
      <div class="image-title-row">
        <div class="image-title" id="image-title"></div>
        <div class="nav-buttons">
          <button id="prev-btn" onclick="previousImage()">←</button>
          <span class="image-counter" id="counter">1 / 5</span>
          <button id="next-btn" onclick="nextImage()">→</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="workflow">
  <div class="container" data-theme="light">
    <h2>From Model to Results</h2>
    <p>Every simulation follows the same seven steps.</p>

    <ol class="workflow-steps">
      <li>
        <strong>Model</strong>
        Import a STEP, DXF, GDS or Python file. Planar files get a layer
        stack-up.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Materials</strong>
        Create materials and assign one to every solid.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Ports</strong>
        Add wave ports on faces, sketch lumped ports, or draw layout ports.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Settings</strong>
        Set the refinement frequency and mesh options, then add frequency sweeps
        and far-field sweeps.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Validate and run</strong>
        Check the setup, run it, and follow the solver progress in the console.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Results</strong>
        Plot fields, S-parameters and patterns, and export what you need.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Iterate</strong>
        Copy a variant, change the design and compare results on the same axes.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="applications" class="features-section">
  <div class="container" data-theme="dark">
    <h2>Applications</h2>
    <p>
      WaveFEM is designed to handle a wide range of electromagnetic simulation
      challenges across multiple industries and research domains.
    </p>

    <div class="grid">
      <article>
        <h3>High-Speed PCB Design</h3>
        <p>
          Analyze signal integrity, crosstalk, and transmission lines in
          multi-layer PCBs for high-speed digital applications.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Semiconductor Design</h3>
        <p>
          Simulate MMICs, RF chips, and packaging interconnects with accurate
          parasitic modeling and high-frequency performance analysis.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Antenna Design</h3>
        <p>
          Design patch antennas, dielectric resonator and Vivaldi antennas, and
          antenna arrays with radiation pattern prediction.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Waveguide Components</h3>
        <p>
          Simulate bandpass filters, adapters and multiplexers with precise
          S-parameter calculations for satellite and radar systems.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="documentation">
  <div class="container" data-theme="light">
    <h2>Documentation</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article>
        <h3><a href="/assets/manual.pdf">User Manual (PDF)</a></h3>
        <p>
          From importing a model to exporting results, with worked examples.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3><a href="/assets/comparison_report.pdf">Validation Report (PDF)</a></h3>
        <p>
          WaveFEM compared against Ansys HFSS on filters, antennas and planar
          circuits.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
